  "id": "COMPOUND:26949 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound 1-(3-Oxo-undecyldisulfanyl)-undecan-3-one and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, as it is identified as a target of multiple entities that ultimately interact with this complex. Specifically, the compound is linked to LoVo, a cell line that is targeted by 3-Hydroxy-7A-Methyl-1Ah-Naphtho[2,3-B]Oxirene-2,7-Dione and by (Z)-alpha-Atlantone and Mansonone E. These latter compounds are also known to target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, indicating a possible pathway through which the compound may exert its effects. The scores assigned to these relationships are consistent, suggesting a plausible mechanism of action. The evidence supports the idea that the compound may modulate the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, potentially through interactions with its target proteins. The strength of the evidence is moderate, and further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct interaction.",
